# Privacy Policy – DataCenter Idle

*Last updated: November 9, 2026*

DataCenter Idle is developed by an independent developer. This policy explains what data the game uses, why, and how you can control it. The game contains **no ads** and does **not** use the advertising ID.

## 1. Data we collect

**Nickname and leaderboard (visible to other players)**
To show the leaderboard and the friends feature, the game stores on Google Firebase: the nickname you choose, your production speed, your total money earned, your current tier, your skin, your online status, your friends list and friend requests. This information is linked to a random identifier created by the game. **Your nickname and these game stats are visible to other players.** Do not use your real name as a nickname.

**Sign-in**
The game signs you in automatically with Firebase Authentication, either anonymously or with your Google Play Games account if you use it. This sign-in is only used to make sure that only you can modify your own data.

**Cloud save**
If you are signed in with Google Play Games, your progress (machines, storage box, rack layout, money and upgrades) is saved on Firebase and linked to your Google Play Games account, so you can restore it on another device.

**Crash reports**
When the game crashes, Firebase Crashlytics sends a technical report: the error, device model, Android version, game version, the game's random identifier and your nickname. These reports are only used to fix bugs.

**Usage statistics (optional)**
On first launch, the game asks whether you agree to send anonymous statistics. If you accept, the game sends Google Analytics for Firebase information about how you play: progress (tiers), in-game actions (buying a machine, opening a lootbox, repairing), session length, device model, OS and game versions, and approximate country. This data contains no nickname, no email address and no advertising ID, and is only used to improve the game. If you decline, nothing is sent. You can change your choice at any time in **Settings › Statistics**; declining stops sending and erases the statistics data stored on the device.

**Former email accounts**
Earlier versions of the game offered an optional account with an email address. This feature is no longer available. Existing data is kept until you ask for its deletion.

## 2. Who processes the data

All data is stored and processed by **Google Firebase** (Google LLC), which acts as our service provider. We do not sell your data and do not share it with anyone else. Google's privacy policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

## 3. Security and retention

Data is encrypted during transfer. Access rules on the database prevent other players from modifying your data.
- Leaderboard, friends and cloud save: kept as long as you play, or until you ask for deletion.
- Crash reports: kept 90 days.
- Usage statistics: kept 14 months.

## 4. Your rights

Under the GDPR, you can access, correct or delete your data at any time. To delete your data, follow these instructions: https://github.com/datacenteridle/DataCenter-Idle/blob/main/account%20deletion — or write to us. You can also lodge a complaint with your data protection authority.

## 5. Contact

